'' THE THREE WAYS '#foreignlib' IS WRONG, each matching one of fbc's own errors --
'' 376, 377 and 378, which its test suite writes as expected-error files.
''
'' STATIC or DYNAMIC is MANDATORY and never inferred from what is on disk: the same
'' directory may hold both an archive and an import library, and choosing by luck
'' would make the build depend on which was made last.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --parse-only %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0328
'' EXPECT-OUT: expected STATIC or DYNAMIC after the #foreignlib name, BADKIND

'' A spec that resolves to nothing lists what was tried, because a silent failure
'' across four variants times three extensions is not a debuggable afternoon.
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0329
'' EXPECT-OUT: found no matching library file

#foreignlib BADKIND "src/vendor/probe"
#foreignlib NOPE static "src/vendor/nothing-here"
print "x"
